$ man ld 2>/dev/null | col -b | grep -n -A22 '^ *--as-needed' | head -26
1362:     --as-needed
1363-     --no-as-needed
1364-	 This option affects ELF DT_NEEDED tags for dynamic libraries mentioned
1365-	 on the command line after the --as-needed option.  Normally the linker
1366-	 will add a DT_NEEDED tag for each dynamic library mentioned on the
1367-	 command line, regardless of whether the library is actually needed or
1368-	 not.  --as-needed causes a DT_NEEDED tag to only be emitted for a
1369-	 library that at that point in the link satisfies a non-weak undefined
1370-	 symbol reference from a regular object file or, if the library is not
1371-	 found in the DT_NEEDED lists of other needed libraries, a non-weak
1372-	 undefined symbol reference from another needed dynamic library.
1373-	 Object files or libraries appearing on the command line after the
1374-	 library in question do not affect whether the library is seen as
1375-	 needed.  This is similar to the rules for extraction of object files
1376-	 from archives.	 --no-as-needed restores the default behaviour.
1377-
1378-	 Note: On Linux based systems the --as-needed option also has an affect
1379-	 on the behaviour of the --rpath and --rpath-link options.  See the
1380-	 description of --rpath-link for more details.
1381-
